rota lap 4431, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; read the threshold, TAME Core, Single-Stranded, and Gauge Style. The reading surfaced two boundaries in the operator guide: who owns a stop file, and whether a helper call reads or acts.
obs Updated the fleet tutorial's stop table and signal-helper paragraphs to match the current scripts. A hand sets .loop-clockout; the agent uses .loop-gates-only for custody gates. A bare fleet_call reports; --signal requests action, and --dry-run forces a preview in either order.
obs The tutorial's automatic card read A 96 while those two claims contradicted the code. Judged Truth 50 made it F 59. A checkpoint preserves its prior wording; after the repair the page reads A 96 with Truth 100. The existing fleet_clockout and fleet_call witnesses pass.
obs Audited all 16 stashes without applying or deleting one. All 13 parked records are carried. The scan reports no work orphans, three moved tools, seven shelf paths, and 62 existing-path edits it cannot judge by presence. The prior recovery's decisions remain recorded in its log.
obs Searched tracked citations for all seven shelf names. Six have none. The September 6 log names the remaining address. Its parked REDS row body matches the published row's 2649 bytes exactly; restored that address as a forwarding page, preserving the published row once and the original stash whole.
obs The detached cold request refused run_in_flight and preserved the existing transcript. Resolved PID 4005947's stdout to session-output/standing-equipment-cold-scoped.txt and checked its 16 stash entries against this checkout. That inherited pass opened at b60b0b3f98 before the previous lap's rebase. Held tracked files still until it finished: 184 green, zero red, two gated, but tree_moved=yes rejects the receipt.
obs The first hot detached launch ended with its tool shell after printing only the launch header. Restarted with a live parent monitor, using the returned transcript path and waiting for its final verdict.
obs The first running hot pass found my missing recital entry: the forwarding filename raised unrecorded_shelves from 62 to 63. Stopped that failed roster with fleet_call --pid 3319082 --signal TERM, waited for its lock to release, and added the recovery entry before restarting the full pass. The guard ceiling stays 62.
obs Both remotes were pulled before writing. The full staged hot pass is the remaining send check; its final counts will be recorded in the commit body because this log is written before that pass. No peer files moved. Room migrations, scrub caching, seed publishing, and custody rulings retain their gates.
